   "evidence": "Mathlib `Distribution.mapCLM` (Distribution.lean:153-188) needs only `[AddCommGroup F'] [Module \u211d F'] [TopologicalSpace F'] [IsTopologicalAddGroup F'] [ContinuousSMul \u211d F']`. `ContinuousLinearMap.toSpanSingleton` (ContinuousLinearMap/Basic.lean:738-743) needs only `[ContinuousSMul R\u2081 M\u2081]`. `delta y : \ud835\udcd3'(\u03a9', \u211d)` (Distribution.lean:201). The `Pushforward` section already assumes exactly these instances on `G`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Distribution/CutoffPushforward.lean",
   "fix": "Add, for the section's general `G`, `cutoffPushforwardCLM_const : (cutoffPushforwardCLM \u03c7 (fun _ \u21a6 y) hc T : \ud835\udcd3'(\u03a9', G)) = mapCLM (ContinuousLinearMap.toSpanSingleton \u211d (T \u03c7)) (delta y)`, proved by `ext g; simp [delta_apply]`.",
   "issue": "`cutoffPushforwardCLM_const_apply` only gives the value `g y \u2022 T \u03c7` at a test function, so a constant-map pushforward cannot be rewritten inside distribution-level predicates (`dsupport`, `waveFrontSet`). The roadmap lists the constant map to a point as a \u00a79.2 check. The reason for declining (that the right-hand side needs a normed `G`) is incorrect.",
